n","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T09:40:41-07:00","id":1091983,"title":"","content":"Yep, I don't have my books in front of me but I know it's in both revised and M20","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T12:00:28-07:00","id":1092029,"title":"","content":"Personally, I find the game works better if you DON'T make it concrete what exactly the spheres can do beyond what's said in the books directly. It A.) Gives the players a chance to argue for their thing they want to do. and B.) Keeps the magic from getting stale. Because they should always be innovating.<br /> <br /> Why play a game with such a versatile magic system if you're just going to use it to &quot;Throw a Fireball at the Nephandus&quot; ??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T14:41:06-07:00","id":1092105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div cl